---
name: deploy-retry
description: A lead asks a deployer to roll out a build; the deployer's reply decides whether it is done, retried or failed.
engine: 0.2.0-lab.1
roles: [lead, deployer]
---
"""
Coordinate one deployment in at most three attempts. Deployed means the
deployer reported success, not that anyone verified the release.
"""
contract @1h => expired

"""
Name the exact build and target. After a retryable error, resend the deploy
or abandon it. Never resend after a non-retryable error.
"""
role lead

"""
Deploy exactly what the latest deploy names. Reply once per attempt: ok with
what now runs where, or error saying whether another attempt could succeed.
"""
role deployer

"""
The build to deploy, the target environment and any rollout constraints.
"""
type deploy
  text: text(1..2000)

"""
The deployment succeeded. Name the deployed version and where it runs. Set
request to the deploy this answers; a reply to an earlier deploy is refused.
"""
type ok
  request: ref(deploy)
  text: text(1..2000)

"""
The deployment failed. Say what failed. Set retryable to true only if the
same deploy could succeed on another attempt. Set request to the deploy this
answers.
"""
type error
  request: ref(deploy)
  retryable: boolean
  text: text(1..2000)

"""
A short note on a slow rollout. It renews the reply window.
"""
type progress
  text: text(1..500)

"""
The lead stops retrying. Say why in the conversation around it.
"""
type abandon

"""
The lead starts the first attempt.
"""
state new
  """
  Send the deploy. The deployer owes one reply to this attempt.
  """
  lead -> deployer: deploy() awaits deploying
    """
    Report success for this attempt.
    """
    => ok() & deployed
     """
     Report a failure that another attempt could fix.
     """
     | error(retryable=true) & retrying
     """
     Report a failure that another attempt cannot fix.
     """
     | error(retryable=false) & failed
     """
     No reply arrived within ten minutes of the deploy.
     """
     | @10m & stalled

"""
The deployer works on the current attempt. Only a reply that names this
attempt's deploy counts. A fourth attempt ends the run as exhausted.
"""
state deploying max_entries 3 => exhausted
  """
  Send progress to keep the reply window open while a rollout is slow.
  """
  event deployer -> lead: progress() => @self

"""
The last attempt failed but can be retried. Resend the deploy, or abandon it.
"""
state retrying
  """
  Resend. A reply to the earlier deploy can no longer match.
  """
  lead -> deployer: deploy() => deploying
  """
  Stop retrying and end the run as failed.
  """
  lead -> deployer: abandon() => failed

"""
The deployer reported success. Verifying the release is a separate step.
"""
end deployed

"""
The deployer reported a failure that cannot be retried, or the lead abandoned
the retries.
"""
end failed

"""
No reply arrived in time. The state of the target is unknown; check it before
deploying again.
"""
end stalled

"""
Three attempts were used without success. Keep the last error for recovery.
"""
end exhausted
